// Original Author: Yannick Casamatta (yannick.casamatta@thalesgroup.com)
//
// RTL sources of the CVA6 Xilinx FPGA top level (`ariane_xilinx`), read by
// the `vivado-fpga-build` recipe through
// `config/target/<target>/Flist.cva6_fpga`.
//
// Self-contained on purpose: it does NOT `-F core/Flist.cva6`. The FPGA build
// substitutes several core files by FPGA-specific ones declaring the very same
// modules (`tc_sram_wrapper`, `hpdcache_sram_1rw`,
// `hpdcache_sram_wbyteenable_1rw`), and drops the behavioural SRAMs and the
// instruction tracer altogether. A filelist can add but not subtract, so
// including the core list would hand Vivado duplicate module definitions and
// let elaboration order decide which one wins - silently producing a bitstream
// built on behavioural memories. The files are therefore listed explicitly,
// and the excluded ones are simply absent.
//
// Excluded here, present in core/Flist.cva6 (the `fpga_filter` and
// `xil_debug_filter` of the root Makefile):
//   common/local/util/tc_sram_wrapper.sv              -> tc_sram_fpga_wrapper.sv
//   hpdcache .../behav/hpdcache_sram_1rw.sv           -> common/local/util/
//   hpdcache .../behav/hpdcache_sram_wbyteenable_1rw.sv  -> common/local/util/
//   hpdcache .../behav/hpdcache_sram_wmask_1rw.sv     -> unused on FPGA
//   vendor/.../tech_cells_generic/src/rtl/tc_sram.sv  -> unused on FPGA
//   common/local/util/instr_tracer.sv                 -> simulation only
//   core/include/instr_tracer_pkg.sv                  -> simulation only
//   corev_apu/riscv-dbg/src/dm_obi_top.sv, dm_pkg.sv,
//   dmi_vjtag_tap.sv, dmi_vjtag.sv                    -> AXI/JTAG debug on FPGA
//
// The zero stage bootloader (`bootrom_<XLEN>.sv`) is NOT listed: it is
// generated by the recipe (cross-compiled, board dependent) and added to the
// Vivado source set from its build directory.
//
// Order matters: packages first, then the design. It reproduces the order the
// root Makefile fed Vivado with.

